    {
      role: 'system',
      content: '[AVERETH ENGINE — authoritative game state, turn 25. Numbers, rolls, positions and knowledge below are binding; narrate, never recalculate.]\n' +
        "Day 2, 06:20 (early morning) | Dyers' yard, Valedorn Crown | mode: story\n" +
        'Setting: Western-fantasy medieval material culture with mana/high magic; letters and messengers for distance; no modern technology.\n' +
        '\n' +
        'Alaric — Level 1 Mage (three-class rules), Power Rank F, Guild Novice | HP 80/80 (unhurt) MP 72/72 STA 100/100\n' +
        "STR 5 VIT 5 AGI 5 INT 6 PER 5 WIL 6 | Equipped: Simple Traveler's Clothes, Starter Arcane Staff, Starter Light Robes\n" +
        "Carried: Small Pouch, Guild plate, Guild contract slip: Clear the Old Crown Catacombs, Level 1, Guild contract slip: Escort the Dyer's Cart to Reedford, roll and hard sausage (portion) | Coin 6 Silver 4 Copper\n" +
        '\n' +
        'ACTIVE SCENE — canonical handles (use these exact handles to distinguish or target actors; card knowledge is authoritative relevant recall, not an exhaustive mind dump):\n' +
        "• Tam [npc.tam] — person, driver of the dyers' cart to Reedford; old man with white stubble and hands like tree roots, checks the harness buckle by buckle, tells Alaric to sit on the left bench and watch the road; SHORT\n" +
